## The design is wrong, ambiguous or impossible

Stop. Do not improvise or commit a half-implementation. Write the exception
document: quote the design, state precisely what is wrong, ambiguous or
impossible, show the evidence — the function that is not there, the two
readings that lead to different code — and propose a clarification or
alternative.

A designer then rules: first whether the problem is real, then whether
anything must change, then what the right change is regardless of your
proposal. Implementation is stopped throughout.

A toolchain failure — missing compiler, missing package manager — is the same
kind of stop. Report it; never install or work around it.

